if (current_hash != last_hash) and (loop_counter == 0):
    state = "AWAKE"
    if (state == "AWAKE"): emit_byte(0x89, "HOLDING")
```
Sprout compares its current memory snapshot against the last one. If they differ, it proves it isn't repeating a loop. Only then does it set the "AWAKE" flag and write the byte. A hang would see identical hashes and never reach the emit line. The math guarantees the receipt is real.
